WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
[music]

2
00:00:05.666 --> 00:00:08.800
[Instructor] All right. Cool. 
We've got some really good Effects

3
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.300
happening right now. If we press Play,
you can see

4
00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:14.966
you can see that we have dirt that comes
out when the Player runs.

5
00:00:14.966 --> 00:00:17.000
And then they jump,
the dirt stops.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.133
They land, the dirt starts again.

7
00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:21.266
And then when they run
into one of the barriers,

8
00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:23.666
a huge puff of smoke comes out.

9
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.533
Now to really finish out this game,

10
00:00:26.533 --> 00:00:29.266
and give it that nice last
bit of polish that it needs,

11
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.400
we're actually going to add
"Sounds," and some "Music."

12
00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:37.100
What we're going to do is 
if you go to your "Main Camera."

13
00:00:40.633 --> 00:00:44.766
Now on your Main Camera,
there is a very interesting

14
00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:48.566
Component on the Camera
called an "Audio Listener."

15
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.833
Much like you need ears
to hear in the real world,

16
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.966
or on a camera you need
a microphone,

17
00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.100
in Unity, you need to add
an Audio Listener

18
00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.366
to be able to hear sounds
in the environment.

19
00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:06.100
Now another thing that we
can to our Main Camera,

20
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.600
if we go to "Add Component,"

21
00:01:09.933 --> 00:01:14.333
if I actually type in "Audio,"
you see there's all these options.

22
00:01:14.466 --> 00:01:17.500
And in fact, we can actually
add in an "Audio Source."

23
00:01:20.466 --> 00:01:23.900
Our Audio Source is actually
where we can get Audio

24
00:01:24.366 --> 00:01:26.400
like clips of Music

25
00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:29.733
or Sound Effects to actually play.

26
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.766
We're going to go
into our Library again,

27
00:01:32.866 --> 00:01:34.666
of our course.

28
00:01:34.666 --> 00:01:38.300
In our "Course Library," you should
actually see a sound Folder.

29
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.400
So if we expand that...

30
00:01:42.633 --> 00:01:45.733
Now we have two options
for Music or Sound Effects.

31
00:01:45.733 --> 00:01:47.766
In this case, we're going to add
some Music.

32
00:01:48.833 --> 00:01:51.466
And there's 3 different
options that we can Play from.

33
00:01:52.166 --> 00:01:55.666
You can see when you click
on one of the Effects,

34
00:01:56.233 --> 00:01:59.500
if we press Play
in our little preview,

35
00:02:00.933 --> 00:02:06.433
[cool game music]

36
00:02:06.933 --> 00:02:08.933
That beat's really cool.

37
00:02:09.366 --> 00:02:11.433
Let's see if we do the second one.

38
00:02:12.366 --> 00:02:15.533
[dark game music]

39
00:02:15.533 --> 00:02:17.633
That one's a little...
a little darker themed.

40
00:02:17.633 --> 00:02:19.766
We're not in a nighttime course,

41
00:02:19.766 --> 00:02:21.766
but that would be really cool.

42
00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.800
Or our last one...

43
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.900
[happy game music]

44
00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.233
This one definitely screams

45
00:02:30.233 --> 00:02:32.666
happy forest.

46
00:02:32.666 --> 00:02:35.566
We're actually going to use
this Sound Effect,

47
00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.766
and we're going to go
to our Main Camera.

48
00:02:39.866 --> 00:02:42.666
I believe it was that
third clip of music.

49
00:02:43.066 --> 00:02:46.033
We'll actually drag
this to our "Audio Source."

50
00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:48.966
Now when we press Play,

51
00:02:48.966 --> 00:02:51.500
we should just hear some music
playing in the background.

52
00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:56.000
[happy game music]

53
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.933
Not bad. Sounds really good.

54
00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.300
Now one thing we want
to make sure is

55
00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.700
it seemed like a pretty short
clip itself.

56
00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.400
It's like 48 seconds.

57
00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.933
If the Player makes it that far,
then the music will just end

58
00:03:09.933 --> 00:03:11.766
so we definitely don't
want that to happen.

59
00:03:11.766 --> 00:03:14.000
If we go to the Main Camera,
we can actually just "Loop."

60
00:03:14.666 --> 00:03:19.066
And then it was a little bit loud 
so we'll just turn it down maybe to...

61
00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:22.400
Do like... 0.6 is probably fine.

62
00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.033
So 60%.

63
00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:27.666
So now when we Play our game,

64
00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:30.566
again, we'll hear
the Music one more time.

65
00:03:30.566 --> 00:03:32.800
It should be a bit quieter.
[happy game music]

66
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.666
Not bad. Just set it down 
a little bit

67
00:03:35.666 --> 00:03:37.700
so that way when
we add Sound Effects,

68
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.733
we'll be able to hear
the Sound Effects over the Music.

69
00:03:40.733 --> 00:03:42.733
Otherwise,
the music might be too loud.

70
00:03:42.733 --> 00:03:45.633
[happy game music]

71
00:03:46.566 --> 00:03:49.433
Cool. With that,
what you're going to do

72
00:03:49.433 --> 00:03:51.733
is you're going to go
to your Main Camera.

73
00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:56.100
You're going to Add a Component
for an Audio Source.

74
00:03:56.766 --> 00:03:59.733
And then you're going to go
into the Assets Folder,

75
00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:01.733
go to the Course Library.

76
00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:04.033
Under Course Library,
go to Sound.

77
00:04:04.933 --> 00:04:07.566
Under Sound, we'll go
into the Music Folder.

78
00:04:07.566 --> 00:04:09.833
You can pick one of
the three bits of music

79
00:04:09.833 --> 00:04:12.233
that you really like.
And then,

80
00:04:12.533 --> 00:04:14.600
in our Main Camera,

81
00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.866
just make sure that you click

82
00:04:16.866 --> 00:04:18.800
and drag whichever
Music you want

83
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.200
into the Audio Source.

84
00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:24.033
And then make sure that you click Loop,
and then you can adjust the Volume

85
00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:26.233
to be however loud or quiet
that you want.

86
00:04:26.433 --> 00:04:27.266
Now it's your turn.

87
00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:31.200
[music]
